content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-114 - AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-20500, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing vibration of 8.3 mm/s is above the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary in manual Figure 3. It therefore falls in Zone D (red, 7.1 to 11.0 mm/s RMS), labelled 'Damage likely - stop the pump'. The manual requires the highest bearing-housing reading to be classified with Figure 3 and acted on by zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Site standard SSP-07 also applies to this reading. Vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone (Zone D) requires stopping the machine immediately and notifying the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The drive-end bearing housing temperature of 70 C is at the upper limit of the manufacturer's normal band ('Normal up to 70 C'). It is below the 80 C alarm and the 90 C trip. Temperature is measured on the housing surface, consistent with the report.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Because the temperature does not exceed the 80 C alarm, the SSP-07 rule that bearing temperature above the alarm limit requires a P1 work order is not triggered. P1 priority is set instead because of the Zone D vibration and the mandatory immediate stop.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported. The shaft-seal leakage symptom in the troubleshooting table is therefore not present, and seal replacement is not indicated by the symptoms.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. It is listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, and the housing temperature is at the top of its normal band.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear. It is listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, and the high reading is at the drive-end housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation (insufficient NPSH).",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop pump P-114 immediately, because the vibration is in Zone D. Notify the reliability engineer. Do not restart until the reliability engineer has cleared the restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any work inside the pump, apply the following controls: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC; close and isolate the suction and discharge valves; obtain a line-break permit; then drain and vent the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm. Record the as-found values.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings. If either the drive-end bearing (6312-C3) or the non-drive-end bearing (6310-C3) shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the impeller for imbalance or damage. This requires removing the back pull-out assembly (68 kg), using certified lifting equipment under a signed lifting plan. Replace the casing gasket HF3-120 whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C05",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check NPSH (suction conditions) to rule out cavitation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, tighten all fasteners to Table 5 of the manual, which is applicable because this serial is below HF3-22000. The Table 5 torque values are not in the evidence provided and must be obtained before work starts.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Re-check alignment with the laser tool after any work that moved the motor or the bearing housing. The tolerances are 0.05 mm parallel and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Once the reliability engineer has authorised the restart, measure vibration on both bearing housings. Classify the highest reading against Figure 3 and confirm it is out of Zone D before returning the pump to service.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 (replace as a pair with HF3-510 if worn)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (replace as a pair with HF3-512)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket - replace whenever the casing is opened (e.g. back pull-out for impeller inspection)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump immediately because of the Zone D vibration. Notify the reliability engineer before any restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Line-break permit; drain and vent before opening.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly is 68 kg, which exceeds the 25 kg threshold. A lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are therefore required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician. This applies to the as-found check, and to re-alignment after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Only if the seal is found damaged or has to be disturbed: mechanical seal replacement, 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Service bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes seal HF3-450 with cartridge seal HF3-450B (gland torque 30 Nm), but only for HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above. P-114 is serial HF3-20500, which is below HF3-22000. The bulletin therefore does not apply to this pump. If the seal is ever disturbed, use HF3-450 and manual Table 5; do not use HF3-450B or the 30 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The manual (Zone D: 'stop the pump') and site standard SSP-07 (highest severity zone: stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer) agree. SSP-07 adds the reliability-engineer notification and restart hold, and both apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Manual Table 5 fastener torque values (including the HF3-450 seal gland torque) are not in the evidence provided.",
    "The report does not state whether 8.3 mm/s is an RMS value, as Figure 3 is based on mm/s RMS.",
    "The non-drive-end bearing housing vibration reading and temperature were not reported.",
    "No labour time is given for back pull-out removal or impeller inspection.",
    "Suction and NPSH data needed to assess cavitation are not available.",
    "It is not stated whether the raw-water transfer line is chemically dosed, which would require chemical goggles and nitrile gloves.",
    "No vibration or temperature trend history is available to judge how fast the condition is deteriorating.",
    "The manual's acceptance criteria for impeller condition and bearing wear are not given in the evidence."
  ]
}
